  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\begin{array}{c|c|c}\r\n\\hline Species & Atomic number & Number of electrons \\\\\r\n\\hline \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+} & 20 & 20-2=18 \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{Cl}^{-} & 17 & 17+1=18 \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{s}^{2-} & 16 & 16+2=18 \\\\\r\n\\hline\r\n\\end{array}\r\nFor isoelectronic species, an increase in atomic number, result in decreased size. Thus, order of radius will be\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}     < \\mathrm{Cl}^{-} < \\mathrm{S}^{2-}\r\n$$",
